---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Methodology · Kingsworth Research">
<style>
  .page-header { padding: 3rem 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-border); margin-bottom:2rem; }
  .content-section { padding: 1.5rem 0; }
  .content-section p { max-width:700px; line-height:1.8; }
  .step-list { list-style:none; counter-reset:steps; padding:0; margin:1.5rem 0; }
  .step-list li { counter-increment:steps; padding:1rem 0 1rem 3.5rem; position:relative; border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .step-list li::before { content:counter(steps, decimal-leading-zero); position:absolute; left:0; top:1rem; font-family:var(--font-heading); font-size:1.5rem; color:var(--color-accent); font-weight:700; }
</style>

<div class="container">
  <div class="page-header">
    <h1>Our Research Methodology</h1>
    <p style="color:var(--color-muted);margin-top:0.5rem;">A transparent process designed for reproducibility and trust.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="content-section">
    <h2 style="font-size:1.5rem;">How We Work</h2>
    <ol class="step-list">
      <li><strong>Topic Identification:</strong> Research themes emerge from recurring procurement questions, regulatory changes, and market shifts identified through our network of industry contacts.</li>
      <li><strong>Evidence Gathering:</strong> Our analysts collect data from multiple independent sources including vendor documentation, user surveys, public filings, and direct product testing where applicable.</li>
      <li><strong>Critical Evaluation:</strong> Each piece of evidence is assessed against our pre-published evaluation criteria. Sources are ranked by reliability and weighted accordingly.</li>
      <li><strong>Peer Review:</strong> Draft reports are shared with at least one external expert reviewer who verifies conclusions and challenges assumptions.</li>
      <li><strong>Publication:</strong> Final reports include full transparency on methodology, evidence quality, limitations, and potential conflicts.</li>
      <li><strong>Ongoing Updates:</strong> Reports are updated when material new evidence emerges. All changes are logged and dated.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <div class="content-section">
    <h2 style="font-size:1.5rem;">Source Reliability Tiers</h2>
    <ul style="margin-top:1rem; padding-left:1.5rem;">
      <li style="margin-bottom:0.5rem;"><strong>Tier 1 — Primary Data:</strong> Direct quantitative results, verified case studies, first-party user surveys.</li>
      <li style="margin-bottom:0.5rem;"><strong>Tier 2 — Expert Testimony:</strong> Peer-reviewed academic publications, recognised industry authority statements.</li>
      <li style="margin-bottom:0.5rem;"><strong>Tier 3 — Secondary Sources:</strong> Analyst firm research, trade media, publicly available market data.</li>
      <li><strong>Tier 4 — Vendor-Provided Materials:</strong> Marketing collateral, white papers, product documentation (minimum weight).</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>
</BaseLayout>
